; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
; INTENT.contractile — Purpose and scope for Skein.jl
; Helps LLM/SLM agents understand what this repo IS and IS NOT.
;
; Part of the contractile family: MUST, TRUST, DUST, INTENT, ADJUST

; ── Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; INTENT (noun)
;   The purpose contractile. Defines what this repository IS, what it is
;   NOT (anti-purpose), and which architectural decisions are load-bearing.
;   Without INTENT, LLMs drift into scope creep, reverse key decisions,
;   or add features that belong in a different repo.
;
; Scope:
;   INTENT governs the conceptual boundaries of the project — its reason
;   for existing, its domain, and its relationship to the ecosystem.
;   It does NOT specify implementation details (that's MUST and code).
;
; Relationship to other contractiles:
;   - MUST: INTENT explains WHY certain MUSTs exist. If you don't
;     understand a MUST, read INTENT first.
;   - TRUST: The "ask-before-touching" section in INTENT maps directly
;     to TRUST.trust-deny for the most sensitive areas.
;   - ADJUST: INTENT's anti-purpose should include "this software is
;     NOT only for users with perfect vision/hearing/mobility."
;   - DUST: When INTENT changes (repo pivots), related DUST entries
;     should be created for the abandoned direction.
;
; ── End Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────

(intent-contractile
  (version "1.0.0")
  (repo "Skein.jl")

  ; === Purpose (what this repo IS) ===
  (purpose
    "Skein.jl is a lightweight, standalone database layer for knot theory in
    Julia: store knots as Gauss codes (or, with the optional KnotTheory.jl
    extension loaded, as canonical planar diagrams), have their invariants
    computed and indexed automatically on insert, then query, compare,
    import and export them through a small composable API. It exists for
    Julia users who want knot persistence and retrieval to be a solved
    problem — whether they arrive from research, teaching, or from another
    package that needs a knot store."
  )

  ; === Anti-Purpose (what this repo is NOT — prevents scope creep) ===
  (anti-purpose
    "Skein.jl is NOT the KRL stack's engine, substrate or 'compute leg': KRL,
    QuandleDB and Tangle are separate projects that CONSUME this library (see
    INTEGRATION.adoc), and shared knot theory transfers no architecture,
    schema or proof guarantee between them. It is NOT a general-purpose
    database engine — the schema is knot-shaped by design. It is NOT an FFI/ABI
    showcase or a coprocessor/accelerator demo: the Idris2/Zig seam and the
    CUDA/Metal/ROCm/TPU/QPU/NPU/VPU/PPU/FPGA/DSP/Crypto/Math extensions were
    vestigial scaffolding and were removed (ADR-0001, rsr-profile.a2ml).
    It does NOT aim to replace KnotTheory.jl — it persists and caches what
    KnotTheory computes."
  )

  ; === Key Architectural Decisions That Must Not Be Reversed ===
  (architectural-invariants
    ("Pure Julia over SQLite.jl — no C ABI seam, no coprocessor backends (ADR-0001)")
    ("KnotTheory.jl is a weakdep loaded via a package extension — never a hard dependency (adr-weakdep, 6a2/META.a2ml)")
    ("SQLite schema is versioned and forward-migrating (v1..v4); schema_version never decreases")
    ("Jones polynomial comes from the Kauffman bracket on canonical planar diagrams, never from bare Gauss codes (adr-jones-from-pd, 6a2/META.a2ml)")
    ("No KRL/Tangle-specific types or schema: consumers adapt Skein, never the reverse")
  )

  ; === Sensitive Areas (if in doubt, ask) ===
  (ask-before-touching
    "src/storage.jl schema + migrations — a schema change must be re-grounded
    against this repo's own storage requirements and come with a forward
    migration"
    ".machine_readable/6a2/ — estate checkpoint files; drift is an
    escalation, not an edit (see 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml)"
    "Project.toml [deps] — adding a hard dependency, especially an estate
    package (KnotTheory, AcceleratorGate, Axiom, ...), requires an ADR"
  )

  ; === Ecosystem Position ===
  (ecosystem
    (belongs-to "standalone (hyperpolymath estate member; see rsr-profile.a2ml)")
    (depends-on ("SQLite.jl" "KnotTheory.jl (weakdep, extension trigger)"))
    (depended-on-by ("QuandleDB" "knot researchers' scripts via Pkg.add(url=...)"))
  )
)
